<main class="page"><div class="eyebrow">About the project</div><h1>Understanding Nepal's disaster history.</h1><p class="lead">Nepal Disaster Archive is a public database documenting natural disasters across Nepal to support research, learning, historical understanding, and preparedness.</p><div class="grid"><section class="block"><h2>Data Sources</h2><p>Records are developed from Government of Nepal and NDRRMA reports, the Department of Hydrology and Meteorology, ICIMOD, USGS, UNESCO, scientific research, and other cited authorities.</p></section><section class="block"><h2>Coverage</h2><p>The archive covers earthquakes, floods, landslides, avalanches, glacial lake outburst floods, storms, lightning, drought, heat waves, cold waves, tornadoes, and wildfires across Nepal's recorded history.</p></section><section class="block"><h2>Methodology</h2><p>Records are collected, checked against available sources, cleaned for consistent fields, and categorized by hazard, province, district, date, and location. Uncertain historical figures are identified rather than presented as exact facts.</p></section><section class="block">
    <h2>Disclaimer</h2><p>Historical records may be incomplete, conflicting, or limited by the sources that survive. Casualty figures, dates, magnitudes, and damage estimates may vary between sources. Please review the references attached to each story.</p></section><section class="block">
